description:
Design a button-activated counter circuit that increments a 3-bit count output each time the button input is pressed, while cycling through a 2-bit state variable that transitions between four states (0 to 3) on each button press. The count increments only on the rising edge of the clock when the button is pressed, allowing the module to act as a simple user input counter with state tracking functionality.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input button,
  output reg [2:0] count
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input button,
  output reg [2:0] count
);reg [1:0] state;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (button) begin
    count <= count + 1;
    case (state)
      0: state <= 1;
      1: state <= 2;
      2: state <= 3;
      3: state <= 0;
    endcase
  end else begin
    state <= state;
  end
end

endmodule

