Design a 48-bit wide storage register that can hold a value provided on its input. The register has a clock input for synchronization and control signals for clearing and loading data. When the clear signal is asserted, the register resets its output to zero; when the load signal is asserted on the rising edge of the clock, it captures the value from the input. This module serves as a basic register for storing and managing 48-bit data in synchronous digital systems.
