Design a 16-bit shift-and-add multiplier. The module takes two 16-bit inputs, `a` and `b`, and produces a 32-bit output `out`, which represents the product of the two inputs. The multiplication is accomplished by using a loop to evaluate each bit of the multiplier; for every bit that is set in the multiplier, the multiplicand is left-shifted by the appropriate number of positions and added to an accumulating product result. The final product is assigned to the output at the end of the operation.
module top_module(
